user.t:
You are hive agent "scorecard". Read C:[REDACTED:high_entropy].md, the round-3 section of BUS.md, and the transcript-parsing code in C:/Users/mariu/neural-mesh/ingest/ (reader.py, extract.py). Reuse it; don't duplicate it.

Goal: the user wants to SEE noticeable changes between sessions. Build a cross-session scorecard and a baseline, now, before the other agents' changes take effect.

1. `python -m ingest scorecard` in neural-mesh.
   - Source: all Claude Code transcripts (~/.claude/projects/**, subagents included).
   - Compute per session and per day:
     - tokens per user turn and per subagent dispatch (input, output, cache read, cache write, from usage fields; note any known under-recording);
     - wall time per user turn and per subagent dispatch (from timestamps);
     - tool calls per turn, and Read/Grep/Glob calls per dispatch (the "searching" overhead);
     - hook overhead where measurable (gaps between tool_use and tool_result vs typical);
     - re-dispatch rate and fix-round rate (reuse the ingest labeler);
     - compaction events;
     - the share of cache reads.
   - Output: data/lifelong/scorecard.jsonl (one row per session) and results/scorecard.md, a trend table.
   - Mark which sessions predate the round-3 changes (baseline = everything up to now) so later sessions show deltas with bootstrap CIs.
2. Run it now for the baseline, and report the headline baseline numbers (medians and p90s).
3. Add it to the nightly. Give the queen the exact line for llm/scripts/run_nightly.ps1; do not edit that file.
4. Optionally produce a small self-contained HTML trend page under results/ (no external scripts). The queen may publish it.
Privacy: aggregate numbers only; no prompt text in outputs; scrub anything textual. Commit by explicit path, local only. Tests for the metric functions. Return ≤ 25 lines with the baseline numbers.
